<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Llíria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Llíria is a town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, about 25 kilometres north-west of the city of Valencia. Above it rises the hill of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edeta">Tossal de Sant Miquel</a>, site of Edeta, the capital of the Iberian Edetani, and the town continued as the Roman municipium of Edeta, whose baths and sanctuary have been excavated. It is now known for its musical tradition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lliria.jpg" alt="Llíria" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Pelayo2 assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VGeneral_Liria.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
